          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Parallel and Intersecting Lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.441,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From this we can observe:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.137,
            0.825,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the corresponding angles formed by a transversal on a pair of lines are equal to each other, then the pair of lines are parallel to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.216,
            0.846,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose, we have a transversal intersecting two parallel lines. What can be said about the corresponding angles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.263,
            0.259,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.283,
            0.849,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 5.19 has a pair of parallel lines l and m (what is the notation used in the figure to indicate they are parallel?) . Line t is the transversal across these two lines. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are corresponding angles. Take a tracing paper and trace "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on it. Now place this tracing paper over "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and see if the angles align exactly. You will observe that the angles match. Check the other corresponding angles in the figure using a protractor. Are all the corresponding angles equal to each other?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.417,
            0.6,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
